  "kind": "build",
  "title": "# Build: app-voice-commands (Current profile) - land Expenses + voice commands for every app ## Wha…",
  "asked": "# Build: app-voice-commands (Current profile) - land Expenses + voice commands for every app ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"It's voice control too - like I can control it with my voice, right?\" ... \"Anytime I build a new app or port an app like that, it needs to be noted whether it's for the framework development itself, and if so, it needs to build in voice commands for the API and MCP and CLI automatically, so they can be added to Molly and controlled by voice.\" Book to a free named agent (Polo if his card exists, else Reel Rhonda). Register id `app-voice-commands` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. **Fable** for the contract step (s1), Opus for the rest (Brett's standing Fable order, no approval). ## Do - s0 **Land Expenses PR #307** first: update from main, fix the red CI, merge, redeploy console so the expenses_* MCP tools go live. Also fix the 'last save wins' risk: the app's grid save must merge by entry id so API/voice adds aren't overwritten by an open tab. - s1 (Fable) **voice-command contract**: `voice-command@1` (or an extension of the existing command/action registry): phrases + slots per command (e.g. 'add {amount} {category} {date}'), confirmation rules for writes/deletes, generated from each app's API/MCP/CLI commands. App manifest field **`forFramework: true|false`** ('is this app for the framework's own development?'). Schema + both validators + fixtures + PORTING.md; kernel untouched. - s2 **Automatic**: the framework app template, `axf init`, and the build launcher add the field and, when `forFramework` is true, generate voice commands for every API/MCP/CLI command automatically; CI check fails if a forFramework app has a command without voice phrases. - s3 **Molly** registers every app's voice commands and runs them by voice (use AmberX's listener / Gizmo voice when available; text-command box as fallback); say 'what can I say in Expenses?' lists them. - s4 Apply to existing apps: Expenses (forFramework: false? -> ask nothing, default **true** for apps living in this repo unless Brett says otherwise; note it in the report), console, axHub web, AmberX, Molly, Gizmo. - Tests, PRs merge when CI green, redeploy console/Molly/expenses. Never leave tsc/vite/playwright running. Report `_claude/builds/reports/app-voice-commands.md`. Write the rule into `_claude/rules/RULES.md`. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
